-- Repo Grid dropdown (FEAT-lt36 owner round 2): the git and agent view, attached under the centre PG42UQ bar.
--
-- Two views, OVERVIEW first:
--   OVERVIEW  high-level summary tiles (repos, worktrees, specs, Conversations, Claude jobs, tokens, budgets), the agent
--             DIAGRAM (repo -> Conversation -> subagent / Claude job, drawn with orthogonal connectors; connector
--             thickness follows tokens) and a right rail with today's top token repos and the budgets nearest their limit.
--   DETAILS   the full lists: AGENTS, REPOS (worktrees, specs), TODAY · TOKENS BY REPO, TASK BUDGETS.
--
-- Owner round 2 note: keep the diagram (main tab with the high-level summary, details second), highlights must go away
-- when the pointer leaves, premium look, "maybe just do the borders". So every highlight is a border: rows, nodes,
-- tiles and cards keep a constant fill, and hover / keyboard selection change only the hairline border colour.
--
-- Hover-clear rule: the Noctalia reconciler applies `fill` / `border` only when the prop is present. A render that drops
-- the prop leaves the previous colour on screen, which is what kept highlights lit after the pointer left. Every
-- highlightable node therefore always sends `border` (and a constant `fill`), with CLEAR or a rest colour at rest.
--
-- Data: `repo-grid-collect` (read-only collector, schema 1) on open and every 10 s while open; second ticks stop when the
-- panel closes, so nothing runs at idle. The last snapshot is shown at once while the first refresh runs.
-- Round 4: clicking (or Enter on) a DIAGRAM node no longer opens anything. It selects the node (EDGE_SELECT border) and
-- the right rail turns into a STATE pane: kind glyph, title, status chip, a GO-TO glyph button and a CLOSE glyph button,
-- then plain-English facts and sections from `repo-grid-collect --detail <key>` (JSON in chat is rendered as readable
-- lines by the collector). The node's known title shows at once; the detail replaces it when the collector answers, and
-- stale answers are dropped by request number. The pane refreshes on the 10 s tick while it is shown. CLOSE (x) brings
-- the tokens and budgets rail back.
-- GO-TO opens the object in the AI that owns it: Hermes -> `ares-summon --hermes`, Claude job -> `ares-summon --claude`,
-- Codex -> `kitty codex resume`, repo -> `kitty` in its checkout. Enter on an already-selected node is GO-TO.
-- DETAILS tab rows keep their direct-open behaviour: a Conversation or job resumes through `ares-summon`, a Codex
-- session resumes in `kitty`, a worktree opens `kitty` there; summary tiles and "+N more" lines switch to DETAILS.
-- Pop-out: a header glyph opens the grid as a free window (`panel-open liquidtron/repogrid:window`, lt14) and closes the
-- dropdown. Window mode is `panel.isWindow ~= nil and panel.isWindow()`; on lt13 the API is nil, so it is always a
-- dropdown. In window mode the pop-out glyph is hidden, PANEL_STATE_PATH is not written, the bar button is not told, and
-- GO-TO leaves the window open.
-- Keys: Left / Right switch view, Tab switches AGENTS / REPOS in DETAILS (OVERVIEW -> DETAILS in OVERVIEW), Up / Down
-- move, Enter selects / opens, Esc closes (host). The panel itself has no fill: it inherits the shell panel material and glass.
--
-- Colour literals (everything else is a palette role):
--   #ff8c00  amber (dirty / draft / budget >= 80 %)
--   #00ff9f  green (live), #00ff9f73 its 45 % border
--   #505060  dark (not checked out)
--   #00000000 transparent (explicit "no highlight")

